WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
-My first guest
is a talented actress,

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.504
a "New York Times"
best-selling author,

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.972
and a successful entrepreneur

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.274
as the founder
of The Honest Company.

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.977
Please welcome Jessica Alba!

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.412
-♪ Jessica Alba ♪

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:15.781
♪ You can't lie to me ♪

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:19.919
♪ 'Cause you're the founder
of The Honest Company ♪

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.821
♪ Jessica Alba ♪

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.224
♪ What can you not do? ♪

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:27.927
♪ My favorite actress
is raising babies, too ♪

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.129
-Jessica. Welcome. Welcome back.
-Thank you!

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:32.398
-Come on. Isn't it great
to hear an audience?

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:36.403
-Yes. I mean, it feels --

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:39.038
it feels like
it's closer to normal.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:41.040
-Yeah, we're getting back there.
-It feels really good.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.943
-Yeah, and it's only 58 people.
They sound like 8,000 people.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.244
-No, seriously.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:46.813
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.582
-Thank you again. Thank you
so much for coming in studio.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.083
-Yeah, it's my pleasure.

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:54.087
-It means a lot to me
and to everybody out there.

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:56.689
I wanted to wish you
a happy belated birthday.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.025
-Thank you.
-Happy birthday, bud!

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.393
-Thank you.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.393 --> 00:01:03.262
-How did you --
It was a big birthday, right?

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:06.799
-Yes. I turned 40.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.268
-Wow! That's massive.

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.470
-Yeah, it's so weird 'cause,
like, when you're little,

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.208
you're like -- that age
just feels aggressive.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.443
-Yeah.
-I don't know.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:18.645
I don't know how else --

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.780
You're just like,
"That's a grown-ass person."

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.116
That is like,
"Yes, that is what that is."

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.051
And when you're here,
you're like...

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:29.055
"I guess this is what it is."
And it -- Yeah.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:30.723
-And when you're here,
you're like,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.525
"That's very young,
that person."

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.761
I'm like, "Well, I remember
when I was 40."

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.129
-Well, 'cause you're like --
you want to --

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:39.399
You know you have so much more
life out there to live,

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:41.834
but I feel like -- I don't know.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.003
Everything is just
sort of, like, connecting

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:47.407
in a really cool way.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.309
Since you were on our show
last time, you went on this

00:01:50.309 --> 00:01:53.178
hiking trip that I wanted
to ask you about because --

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:54.814
-Oh, geez.
-No, because I think

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.215
that you're in amazing shape.

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:59.919
You're healthy.
And wellness, that's your thing.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.187
And I go, "Great."
-Yes.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.122
-So I think hiking
would be right up your alley.

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.490
-Nope.
-Really?

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.026
-Definitely not.
-Wow. Now, explain it to me.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:11.497
-It was a vegan hiking
detox situation.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:13.365
-Uh-huh.
-And I didn't realize --

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:16.201
So, in my mind, I'm like,
"I'm going there

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:17.870
to do the healthy thing."

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.741
But, actually, you're
supposed to, like, eliminate

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.310
all the things
before you get there.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.781
So, like, for a month, you
should stop drinking alcohol.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.651
-[ Laughter ]
-And I was like, uh...

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.352
-Yeah, have you met
the quarantine?

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:34.820
-The night before, I was like,

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.922
"How many margaritas
can I get in?"

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.291
-You're like, "Oh, the detox
starts a month before the detox?

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:40.927
Oh, interesting."

00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:42.829
-And then they're like,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:47.100
"And you should eliminate meat,
you know, a week or two weeks."

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.203
I was, like, downing tacos
that morning...

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.004
-Wow!
-...with all the things on it.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.007
-So then
you get to this place --

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.342
-So, I get there,
and I guess it just --

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.678
Oh, yeah, and you're supposed to
hike like six miles a day.

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:01.380
Who has time for that?

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.282
-Wait. So this is before
you go on the hike

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.751
you have to do the hike?

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.652
-All of these things.
You're supposed to walk.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:09.688
Walk for like six miles a day.
Build yourself up.

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:12.392
I did not nary. None of it.
Zero.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:16.128
-"Nary." [ Laughs ]
Nary a thing. I love "nary."

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:18.498
-But then we were on the hike,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:21.000
and our first day,
we're halfway up.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.836
We're like, "We don't know
if we can do this anymore."

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:28.574
And then a pack of solid,
solid senior citizens,

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:32.444
like, 80 to 90-year-old sen--
-Yeah, real seniors.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:35.314
-They just, like,
boom, right past us.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:36.916
-Booking.
-Booking.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.818
And we're dying.
-Huffing and puffing.

00:03:39.818 --> 00:03:41.086
-Huffing and puffing.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:42.755
And then they came,
and they lapped us.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.490
They went to the top
and came back down.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.559
And we still
hadn't quite made it up.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:49.528
-Unbelievable! All right.
I want to check this out.

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:50.796
-I was -- Yeah -- Anyway.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.799
One of those moments
where you're like,

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.400
"I might be failing at this.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.036
Whatever this is,
this is not my thing."

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.370
-"Yeah. This is not my thing."
Exactly.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:01.507
I'll tell you what is your
thing. The Honest Company.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.642
Congratulations on this.
-Thank you.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:05.111
-This is a giant thing.
We all --

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.046
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-I use it. I love it.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.148
But this is a big deal.
You just went --

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.983
You rang the bell at NASDAQ,

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:13.453
and you went public
with your stock.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:16.289
That's a giant thing
to happen for a business.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:17.824
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.825
You worked your butt off, buddy.
You worked so hard.

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:21.861
How long have you been doing
that, The Honest Company?

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.130
-So I founded it nine years ago.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.465
-Wow!
-And it's wild.

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:29.835
It's a dream come true.

00:04:29.835 --> 00:04:31.170
I mean, it's --

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:35.073
You always think of, like --
You have this idea --

00:04:35.073 --> 00:04:37.209
And can I really build

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:40.913
this ethical business that
stands for, like, human health

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:44.183
and thinking about the planet
and sustainability

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.952
and diversity and inclusion?

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:51.090
And can a company
that really has purpose do well

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:57.796
and be looked at in the business
world and taken seriously?

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:00.566
-Yeah. Nine years of work.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.401
-Yeah.
-And it really paid off.

00:05:02.401 --> 00:05:04.804
Your family was with you
when you rang the bell.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:06.305
-Yeah.
-Was that emotional?

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:10.209
-Oh, my gosh. I was trying
to keep it together, but, yeah.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:12.278
It's -- It's --

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:15.581
It was one of the most amazing
experiences,

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.783
especially to do that with --

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.152
you know, have my family with me
and my team.

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.754
And it was incredible.

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:24.757
-It's a big deal. Good for you.
Congratulations on that.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:26.625
That's awesome
that you did that.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.226
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.226 --> 00:05:30.796
Every time you come on,
I go, "What's the new thing?

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.898
What's the next thing?
What are we talking about?

00:05:32.898 --> 00:05:34.766
Facemasks. What are we doing?"

00:05:34.766 --> 00:05:36.435
But now you're like, "No.
I'm on to a new mission now."

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:40.506
-Yeah. So, we launched this new
Conscious Cleaning line.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.942
And so we have an alternative
to the traditional

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:45.044
sort of harsh chemicals,

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.813
but it's a disinfecting spray.

00:05:46.813 --> 00:05:48.347
So we have that.

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.216
We also have sanitizing wipes

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.951
that also use
our clean ingredients.

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:56.289
And then we have
three types of home cleaners

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:58.991
that you basically
reuse the bottle,

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.328
and it comes in refills,
and there's a concentrate.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:05.164
So just, like, if you think
of all of the bottles

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:09.101
that go into landfill,
if a couple of choices

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:13.472
that all of us make can be more
thoughtful and more conscious,

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:17.543
then you're just going to
make a giant impact overall.

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:20.579
So I'm really excited that we
launched the Conscious Cleaning.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:22.514
-I love that you're doing
all of this.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:25.317
And a mom. And an actor.

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:28.487
You're fantastic and a great
guest to have on our show.

00:06:28.487 --> 00:06:30.956
Please come back whenever.
You know we love you so much.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.059
-Thank you.
-Jessica Alba, everybody.

